/config/board-slas.json
/public/logo-config.json
/.last-update-check

# ── Deploy / roll artefacts (operator-generated, never committed) ────────────
# WHY THIS SECTION EXISTS. scripts/atomic-deploy.sh, update.sh and the fleet
# roll park pre-deploy copies of live files next to the originals so a bad
# deploy can be reverted (`*.PREDEPLOY-<ts>-keep`, `*.preroll-bak`,
# `.next.CORRUPT-<ts>`, `<db>.backup-<ts>`). They are deliberately NOT deleted.
#
# Left un-ignored, they make `git status --porcelain` permanently non-empty.
# update-skills.sh's CC currency probe (`_cc_currency_probe`) reads a non-empty
# porcelain as `state=dirty` and then, by contract, REFUSES to refresh the
# checkout:
#     "Command Center has UNCOMMITTED changes, so it cannot fast-forward and
#      will NOT be refreshed."
# So a box that deploys once litters itself into permanent staleness: every
# later roll sees `dirty`, skips the CC refresh, and the checkout never
# advances again — while the .onboarding-version stamp stays green.
#
# Ignoring these restores a clean porcelain so the refresh can actually run.
# Only operator/deploy-generated backup copies are listed; every real source
# file (including public/brand.css and the *.example.json templates) stays
# tracked.
*.preroll-bak
*.PREDEPLOY-*-keep
*.PREFIX-*-keep
.PREDEPLOY-*-keep/
.next.PREDEPLOY-*
.next.CORRUPT-*
.next-backup-redeploy/
*.db.backup*
*.db.rogue-preserved*
*.orig
*.rej

# Isolated mock Duck e2e Next build
.next-duck-e2e/
